# Print-in-place fit proofs. `fitcheck` renders every moving/fixed pairwise
# interference — both spinner rotors vs the card+posts, the bead vs the card,
# the hinge pin vs card and flap, and the easel flap vs the card at 0/35/70 deg
# and at the deployed angle — and must be EMPTY (all clearances real on the
# built mesh). `fitcheck_neg` over-rotates the flap past its designed stop and
# MUST interfere: it proves the rotation stop exists AND that the check can
# fail. The bead's breakaway anchor nib is a declared weld (CC2) drawn outside
# the fitcheck bodies — see NOTES.md.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
# Standing per-mechanism proofs (issue #37: a formula that ASSERTs itself
# proves nothing about the built mesh). `fitcheck_spin` intersects each rotor
# with the fixed body (post, cone cap, plate, embosses); its neg raises rotor
# 1 past the axial float (z_tol + 0.2) so the cone cap bites the bore rim.
# `fitcheck_slide` intersects the weld-free bead (the CC2 anchor nib stays
# outside, as in `fitcheck`) with the channel walls, roof, slot and bar; its
# neg shoves the bead sideways by slide_tol + foot_side_clear + 0.2.
fitcheck_spin       empty
fitcheck_spin_neg   interferes
fitcheck_slide      empty
fitcheck_slide_neg  interferes
